  "notes": "Classically-trained complextro turned pop hitmaker, and the research names the training as \"the defining parameter\" — piano from age four, drums from twelve, both parents musicians — \"which shows as genuine voice-leading, secondary dominants and modulating breakdowns inside an EDM frame, rather than the lane's static four-chord vamp\". So this is the only model in the progressive/electro block with `topVoiceStepwise` on, a stepwise-led open voicing, five progression families and a `1_per_bar` harmonic rhythm carrying the weight: the chords move. The drums carry the other half: \"complextro grammar — a four-square kick under glitchy, intricate rhythmic programming, with percussion and bass cut into 16th and 32nd fragments that alternate rather than sustain; he came from deathcore drumming, which shows in the fill density\". That is the highest hat fill density and roll frequency in this section, a 64th in the roll vocabulary, and a four-lane perc bed at 4-8 hits a bar. The bass is \"sawtooth-and-distortion chopped into interlocking 16th fragments\", authored as an independent riff at 0.6 roots with two cell shapes. Loops are 4 or 8 bars. ⚠ The research calls the drum and bass grammar a reading of the complextro description; that mark is repeated here, and all velocities and densities are INFERRED.",
